d": "28e379670a5ffafcc705f16110d8ae84", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "8c2fd4df-cb3b-574c-9630-3dbef8b4ac2b", "at": 1795682132.0600286, "until": 1795682132.2315214, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54166, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "28e379670a5ffafcc705f16110d8ae84", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (74 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "Outline rev 12 is pushed. It carries analysis's paired interval for the larger-gap inner split (`inner50`) from `results/inner50/paired_vs_main.csv`. I sent no new message.\n\n- **Main case:** for `balanced × diff-irt` in extrapolation at n = 100, the paired ratio of `inner50` to the main inner split is 0.936 [0.924, 0.952]. That is a precise 6.4% reduction in RMSE.\n- **Not uniform:**\n  - kNN gets 0.948 [0.931, 0.971].\n  - `strat × diff-irt` gets 0.986 [0.978, 0.999].\n  - The ridge difference estimator gets worse, at 1.094 [1.077, 1.113].\n  - The text will say a larger inner share helps the λ choice for the IRT and kNN predictors, not for ridge.\n- **Standing:** the intervals are over families only, and `inner50` was chosen after seeing the main result. It stays a post-hoc diagnosis.\n\nTwo items are still pending on `experiment-repo`#5, waiting on the host queue: the recalibrated-estimator grid and the R = 100 per-target bias run. I left that request open, and the outline lists both as open."}}, {"id": "1d74734d-9404-5e37-8795-822bcbfc77ea", "at": 1795682132.275132, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 54241, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "28e379670a5ffafcc705f16110d8ae84", "trust": "ag